herolte: the bench switches governors at run time: v2, fixed and the two-state v1 of min100 in one boot (0475)

min100 runs herogov=1 (two states: the big cluster at its rate only while its four cores are busy), which E-0329 never measured: it compared v2 with a fixed rate. hg_policy now selects who moves the cluster (0 none, 1 the power thread's two-state governor, 2 governor v2 or fixed, 3 a switch in progress with nobody moving it), the v2 thread parks and restarts from the real state when it is not the active one, and heroscenc digit 5 means the v1 governor at 1976 MHz. The defaults need no argument: three rounds, paging and spotlight, caps 385 (v2 governed 1976, fixed 1976, v1), labelled paging, paging_fixed and paging_v1. Needs herocpu_mhz=1976 so that v1 goes to 1976. heroscen only.

